<!-- OBVR's "VR" button in the main menu: put into whatever main menu is loaded by MenuQue's
     InsertXML at the menu's top level (game/MainMenuVr.cpp, ui/MainMenuButton.h), so no main
     menu file is shipped or replaced. It is the game's own floating button (the prefab the
     menu's Continue, New, Load ... are made of: its font, its brown on the parchment, its
     highlight), in the row of those buttons (y 725) at the right, clear of Exit at 4:3 and
     wider. Shown with the menu's own buttons (the main menu's user1). A click on it starts
     OBVR's start guide again; the engine's own click handling knows no id 9700 and does nothing
     with it.
     Not the menu's user3 for its alpha: that is the fade of the film logo over the real one, 0
     once the menu stands - the first version's label copied it and was never seen (harness
     main-menu-vr-button 20261116-100010; with 255 it showed, vr-button-sweep 20261116-100344:
     small and pale on the dark border, with no highlight to be seen there). -->
<rect name="obvr_vr">
 <include src="button_floating.xml"/>
 <id>9700</id>
 <visible><copy src="MainMenu" trait="user1"/></visible>
 <string>VR</string>
 <depth>12</depth>
 <x><copy src="screen()" trait="width"/><sub>170</sub></x>
 <y>725</y>
 <clicksound>1</clicksound>
</rect>
